rchitecture/fluid-integration-59","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The class describes how Fluid starts each Curvine role:","locale":"en"},"62":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-60","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Role     | Kubernetes workload | Responsibility                        |\n| -------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `master` | `StatefulSet`       | Curvine metadata and journal service. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"63":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-61","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Role     | Kubernetes workload | Responsibility |\n| -------- | ------------------- | -------------- |\n| `worker` | `StatefulSet`       | Cache storage. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"64":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-62","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Role     | Kubernetes workload | Responsibility                   |\n| -------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `client` | `DaemonSet`         | FUSE mount for application pods. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"65":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-63","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The class also defines `executionEntries.mountUFS`. Fluid calls this entry so Curvine can mount Dataset UFS paths before serving the Dataset. In the Curvine image, the script is:","locale":"en"},"66":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-64","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The script reads `FLUID_RUNTIME_CONFIG_PATH`, runs `cv mount` for non-Curvine UFS paths, skips native `curvine://` paths, and returns JSON in the shape Fluid expects:","locale":"en"},"67":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-65","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The class also defines `executionEntries.ReportSummary`. Fluid calls this entry from the master pod to refresh Dataset cache status. In the Curvine image, the script is:","locale":"en"},"68":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-66","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The script runs:","locale":"en"},"69":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-67","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"It prints strict JSON to stdout, as required by Fluid's ReportSummary contract:","locale":"en"},"70":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-68","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"Curvine reports values that the master can return cheaply: cached bytes, cache capacity, and file count. `ufsTotal`, `cachedPercentage`, and `cacheHitRatio` stay `0` until Curvine has authoritative UFS total and hit-ratio metadata. This avoids showing a cache-capacity percentage as a Dataset cache percentage.","locale":"en"},"71":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-69","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integrati