heruntime-config-is-generated","content":"| Curvine config | Source                                |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `cluster_id`   | Dataset name or Dataset mount option. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"86":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-84","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#how-cacheruntime-config-is-generated","content":"| Curvine config          | Source                                  |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `journal.journal_addrs` | Fluid master topology and service name. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"87":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-85","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#how-cacheruntime-config-is-generated","content":"| Curvine config    | Source                                 |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `worker.data_dir` | Worker options or Fluid `tieredStore`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"88":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-86","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#how-cacheruntime-config-is-generated","content":"| Curvine config        | Source                          |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `client.master_addrs` | Generated master RPC endpoints. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"89":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-87","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#how-cacheruntime-config-is-generated","content":"| Curvine config  | Source                    |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `fuse.mnt_path` | Fluid client target path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"90":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-88","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#how-cacheruntime-config-is-generated","content":"This is why `FLUID_RUNTIME_CONFIG_PATH` is important for master, worker, and client pods.","locale":"en"},"91":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-89","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#dataload-with-cacheruntime","content":"`DataLoad` asks Fluid to preload one or more Dataset paths into the cache. For Curvine, the DataLoad job should eventually run:","locale":"en"},"92":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-90","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#dataload-with-cacheruntime","content":"There are two separate parts:","locale":"en"},"93":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-91","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#dataload-with-cacheruntime","content":"`CacheRuntimeClass.dataOperationSpecs` tells Fluid how to run a DataLoad job for this cache runtime.","locale":"en"},"94":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-92","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#dataload-with-cacheruntime","content":"A `DataLoad` resource asks Fluid to preload paths for a specific Dataset.","locale":"en"},"95":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-93","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"Add `dataOperationSpecs` at the top level of the existing `CacheRuntimeClass`.","locale":"en"},"96":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-94","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"Do not change `topology`, `fileSystemType`, or the master/worker/client definitions just to enable DataLoad.","locale":"en"},"97":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-95","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"Do not copy this snippet as a complete production command unless your DataLoad image or script creates `/etc/curvine.toml` before running `cv load`. The Curvine sample `curvine-docker/fluid/cache-runtime/curvine-cache-runtime-class.yaml` includes that setup logic.","locale":"en"},"98":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-96","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"Fluid injects these environment variables into the DataLoad job:","locale":"en"},"99":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-97","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Variable                  | Meaning                            |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `FLUID_DATALOAD_METADATA` | Whether metadata should be loaded. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"100":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-98","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Variable                   | Meaning                       |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `FLUID_DATALOAD_DATA_PATH` | Paths to load, joined by `:`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"101":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-99","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Variable                       | Meaning                                     |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `FLUID_DATALOAD_PATH_REPLICAS` | Replica count for each path, joined by `:`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"102":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-100","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The Curvine CacheRuntimeClass sample uses an inline DataLoad script because Fluid runs data operations as short-lived Jobs. The script first generates Curvine config from the Fluid runtime JSON. If that file is not mounted, it falls back to Dataset metadata, pod labels, and finally a DataLoad name pattern such as `<dataset>-load`.","locale":"en"},"103":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-101","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"When Fluid passes a Dataset path such as `/minio`, the script checks Curvine mount metadata and resolves it to the real Curvine load source before running `cv load --watch`. This keeps DataLoad aligned with `mountUFS`.","locale":"en"},"104":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-102","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#2-create-a-dataload-resource","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"105":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-103","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#2-create-a-dataload-resource","content":"Apply it:","locale":"en"},"106":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-104","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#2-create-a-dataload-resource","content":"`spec.dataset` selects the Dataset. `spec.target[].path` selects the Dataset path to preload. Fluid passes the target paths to the job through `FLUID_DATALOAD_DATA_PATH`.","locale":"en"},"107":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-105","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#3-check-the-dataload-job","content":"The DataLoad job is successful only if the Curvine load command exits successfully for every target path. If `cv load --watch` returns an error, the job should fail so Fluid can report the problem.","locale":"en"},"108":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-106","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"Fluid chart `helm-chart-fluid-1.1.0-alpha.10` mounts the runtime config file into CacheRuntime DataLoad pods and sets `FLUID_RUNTIME_CONFIG_PATH`. With that version, Curvine DataLoad can generate config the same way as master, worker, and client pods.","locale":"en"},"109":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-107","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"Older Fluid versions or custom DataLoad templates may set `FLUID_RUNTIME_CONFIG_PATH` without mounting the file into the DataLoad pod.","locale":"en"},"110":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-108","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"If your DataLoad command needs the runtime JSON, verify both conditions:","locale":"en"},"111":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-109","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"`FLUID_RUNTIME_CONFIG_PATH` is set in the DataLoad pod.","locale":"en"},"112":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-110","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"The file exists inside the DataLoad pod.","locale":"en"},"113":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-111","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"If the file is missing, Curvine's sample tries these fallbacks in order:","locale":"en"},"114":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-112","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"`CURVINE_DATALOAD_DATASET`, `FLUID_DATASET_NAME`, or `CURVINE_DATALOAD_MASTER_HOST`.","locale":"en"},"115":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-113","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"Fluid pod labels such as `targetDataset` or `fluid.io/dataset-id`.","locale":"en"},"116":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-114","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"DataLoad names derived from the Dataset name, for example `<dataset>-load`.","locale":"en"},"117":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-115","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#about-etcfluidconfigruntimejson","content":"If none of these identify the Dataset, set the Dataset or master host explicitly