architecture-32","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"Workers support **multi-tier storage**:","locale":"en"},"1887":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-33","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**MEM**: In-memory tier (< 100 ns)","locale":"en"},"1888":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-34","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**SSD**: NVMe / SATA (< 100 µs)","locale":"en"},"1889":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-35","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**HDD**: Capacity tier (< 10 ms)","locale":"en"},"1890":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-36","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**SPDK**: User-space NVMe acceleration","locale":"en"},"1891":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-37","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**UFS**: Underlying storage (S3, HDFS, etc.) accessed through Curvine’s data orchestration; Curvine provides a unified file system view over mounted UFS paths and native paths.","locale":"en"},"1892":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-38","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"Supported UFS types include:","locale":"en"},"1893":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-39","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**S3 / MinIO**","locale":"en"},"1894":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-40","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**OSS**","locale":"en"},"1895":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-41","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**HDFS**","locale":"en"},"1896":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-42","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Local FS**","locale":"en"},"1897":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-43","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**OpenDAL (Azure, GCS, etc.)**","locale":"en"},"1898":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-44","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"In addition, Curvine provides foundational components:","locale":"en"},"1899":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-45","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**orpc**: High-performance RPC framework (Tokio-based, zero-copy)","locale":"en"},"1900":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-46","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**curvine-web**: Admin UI and cluster management","locale":"en"},"1901":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-47","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Metrics**: Prometheus-based monitoring (master/worker/client, job, cache)","locale":"en"},"1902":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-48","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"For deployment topology and component roles, see Deployment Architecture. For internal data flow (journal, replay, client read/write), see Basic Architecture.","locale":"en"},"1903":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-49","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"To achieve high performance, high concurrency, and low resource consumption, Curvine adopts the following technologies and design principles:","locale":"en"},"1904":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-50","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**Pure Rust Implementation**: Curvine is implemented entirely in Rust, avoiding performance bottlenecks and resource consumption of traditional languages while ensuring code safety and stability","locale":"en"},"1905":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-51","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**High-Performance RPC Framework**: Curvine implements a custom RPC communication framework supporting efficient data transmission with asynchronous I/O and zero-copy implementation within the framework","locale":"en"},"1906":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-52","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**Zero-Cost Abstractions**: Zero-cost abstraction design where core modules directly interface with underlying systems, avoiding unnecessary abstraction layers and improving system performance and resource utilization","locale":"en"},"1907":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-53","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**Asynchronous I/O**: Asynchronous I/O design fully utilizes system resources, avoiding blocking waits and improving system concurrent processing capabilities","locale":"en"},"1908":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-54","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**Zero-Copy**: Zero-copy design avoids data copying and memory allocation, reducing system memory usage and resource consumption","locale":"en"},"1909":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-55","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"Curvine adopts distributed architecture design with multi-replica mechanisms and failover mechanisms to ensure system high availability:","locale":"en"},"1910":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-56","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"**Raft Protocol**: Uses Raft protocol to implement distributed consistency, ensuring data consistency and reliability","locale":"en"},"1911":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-57","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"**Automatic Failover**: Automatic failover mechanism that switches to backup nodes when primary nodes fail, ensuring system high availability","locale":"en"},"1912":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-58","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"**Multi-Replica Mechanism**: Multi-replica mechanism ensures data redundancy backup, improving system reliability and fault tolerance","locale":"en"},"1913":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-59","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"**Snapshot Mechanism**: Lightweight snapshot mechanism for periodic data backup, improving system recovery speed and stability","locale":"en"},"1914":{"id":"/docs/Overview","page_id":"/docs/Overview","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Overview"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview","locale":"en"},"1915":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","type":"page","content":"Curvine Overview","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Overview"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","locale":"en"},"1916":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-0","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#core-features","content":"Core Features","locale":"en"},"1917":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-1","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#use-cases","content":"Use Cases","locale":"en"},"1918":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-2","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#performance","content":"Performance","locale":"en"},"1919":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-3","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#-modular-architecture","content":"🧩 Modular Architecture","locale":"en"},"1920":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-4","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","content":"Curvine is a high-performance distributed cache system written in Rust and released under the Apache 2.0 license. It provides a unified cached file-system view over external storage systems, with low-latency metadata access, high-throughput data access, and POSIX-compatible FUSE integration.","locale":"en"},"1921":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-5","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","content":"Curvine uses a classic Master/Worker architecture. Master nodes manage metadata and cluster coordination, while Worker nodes store and serve data blocks. Metadata consistency and high availability are provided through Raft.","locale":"en"},"1922":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-6","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","content":"Curvine exposes multiple access paths for analytics, AI, and data infrastructure workloads, including the Rust CLI, FUSE, and Java/Python SDK bindings.","locale":"en"},"1923":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-7","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#core-features","content":"**Multi-cloud storage support**: Works with S3-compatible systems, HDFS, OSS, MinIO, and other UFS backends through a unified access layer","locale":"en"},"1924":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-8","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#core-features","content":"**Cloud-native integration**: Supports CSI-based deployment and Kubernetes-oriented packaging workflows","locale":"en"},"1925":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-9","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#core-features","content":"**Multi-tier cache**: Supports memory, SSD, and HDD cache strategies","locale":"en"},"1926":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-10","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#core-features","content":"**POSIX-compatible access**: Provides a FUSE layer so existing applications can access cached data as a local file system","locale":"en"},"1927":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-11","page_id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/instroduction#core-features","content":"**HDFS ecosystem compatibility**: Offers Hadoop FileSystem integration and SDK access paths","locale":"en"},"1928":{"id":"/docs/Overview/instroduction-12","page_id":"/docs/Over