anuals/Access/s3-gateway-36","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#bucket-not-found","content":"Bucket not found","locale":"en"},"2121":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-37","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#connectivity-check","content":"Connectivity check","locale":"en"},"2122":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-38","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#performance-tuning","content":"Performance Tuning","locale":"en"},"2123":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-39","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","content":"The Curvine S3 gateway exposes a Curvine cluster through an S3-compatible HTTP API. Tools that already speak S3 — the AWS CLI, MinIO Client, boto3, or any S3 SDK — can read and write Curvine paths without FUSE or a native Curvine client. The gateway authenticates each request with AWS Signature V2/V4 and translates bucket and key names into Curvine filesystem operations.","locale":"en"},"2124":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-40","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","content":"The gateway is an optional, standalone service. It is not started by `curvine-server` and is not included in the default release package yet. Build it explicitly with `cargo build --release --bin curvine-s3-gateway` and run it alongside a Curvine cluster.","locale":"en"},"2125":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-41","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#overview","content":"S3 requests enter the gateway, are authenticated against a credential store, and are executed through the Curvine client. Object data streams through the gateway to and from Curvine Workers, so an entire object is never buffered in memory.","locale":"en"},"2126":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-42","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#key-features","content":"S3-compatible bucket and object APIs (see Supported S3 Operations)","locale":"en"},"2127":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-43","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#key-features","content":"AWS Signature V2/V4 authentication with a local or Curvine-hosted credential store","locale":"en"},"2128":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-44","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#key-features","content":"HTTP Range requests with `206 Partial Content` responses","locale":"en"},"2129":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-45","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#key-features","content":"Multipart upload for large objects","locale":"en"},"2130":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-46","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#key-features","content":"Streaming reads and writes","locale":"en"},"2131":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-47","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#key-features","content":"Standalone deployment that can be scaled behind a load balancer","locale":"en"},"2132":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-48","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#architecture-overview","content":"The S3 gateway is the frontend for S3 API clients; it converts S3 requests into Curvine filesystem operations:","locale":"en"},"2133":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-49","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#bucket-operations","content":"| Operation      | HTTP request    |\n| -------------- | --------------- |\n| `CreateBucket` | `PUT /{bucket}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2134":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-50","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#bucket-operations","content":"| Operation    | HTTP request     |\n| ------------ | ---------------- |\n| `HeadBucket` | `HEAD /{bucket}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2135":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-51","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#bucket-operations","content":"| Operation      | HTTP request       |\n| -------------- | ------------------ |\n| `DeleteBucket` | `DELETE /{bucket}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2136":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-52","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#bucket-operations","content":"| Operation     | HTTP request |\n| ------------- | ------------ |\n| `ListBuckets` | `GET /`      |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2137":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-53","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#bucket-operations","content":"| Operation           | HTTP request             |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `GetBucketLocation` | `GET /{bucket}?location` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2138":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-54","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway"