content":"S3 (`s3://`, `s3a://`)","locale":"en"},"2760":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-19","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"OSS (`oss://`)","locale":"en"},"2761":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-20","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"HDFS (`hdfs://`)","locale":"en"},"2762":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-21","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#webhdfs-webhdfs","content":"WebHDFS (`webhdfs://`)","locale":"en"},"2763":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-22","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","content":"This section is based on the current repository source in `curvine-cli`, `build/cv`, and `build/bin/dfs`. Curvine currently exposes three CLI entry styles:","locale":"en"},"2764":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-23","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","content":"**Native Rust CLI `cv`**: the recommended entry point, with the full command tree from `curvine-cli`.","locale":"en"},"2765":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-24","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","content":"**Compatibility wrapper `dfs`**: bundled in the distribution; `fs` / `report` go through Java `CurvineShell` and keep Hadoop `FsShell` style.","locale":"en"},"2766":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-25","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","content":"**POSIX / FUSE**: after mounting with FUSE, use standard Linux commands directly on the mount point.","locale":"en"},"2767":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-26","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"Get a quick overview:","locale":"en"},"2768":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-27","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"The current top-level commands in source are:","locale":"en"},"2769":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-28","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"All `cv` commands accept these global options:","locale":"en"},"2770":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-29","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"| Global option   | Description                                                                                                                       |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--conf <PATH>` | Override the cluster config file for this invocation. If omitted, the CLI uses its normal configured path or `CURVINE_CONF_FILE`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2771":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-30","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"| Global option            | Description                                                                           |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--master-addrs <ADDRS>` | Override the client-side master address list directly, for example `m1:8995,m2:8995`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2772":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-31","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"Normal production commands use `cv` directly because the cluster configuration\nis already installed or selected through `CURVINE_CONF_FILE`. Use `--conf` only\nto select a non-default configuration, for example during migration or\ndiagnosis. `cv mount --config key=value` remains the UFS-property option.","locale":"en"},"2773":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-32","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"**Conventions:**","locale":"en"},"2774":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-33","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"In production, add the distribution `bin/` directory to `PATH` and invoke `cv` directly.","locale":"en"},"2775":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-34","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"When run via `cargo run -p curvine-cli -- ...`, the help output shows the binary name as `curvine-cli`.","locale":"en"},"2776":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-35","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"Items such as `<PATH>` and `<JOB_ID>` are positional arguments; `[OPTION]` means optional.","locale":"en"},"2777":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-36","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"**Usage:** `cv report [json|all|capacity|used|available]`","locale":"en"},"2778":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-37","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command     | Description                                                                               |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv report` | Default summary, including active master, capacity, inode/block counts, and worker lists. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2779":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-38","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command          | Description                         |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `cv report json` | Emit the full `MasterInfo` as JSON. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2780":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-39","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command                              | Description                                            |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `cv report all --show-workers false` | Text summary, with optional worker detail suppression. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2781":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-40","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command                               | Description                                                      |\n| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv report capacity [WORKER_ADDRESS]` | Show cluster-wide capacity, or detailed capacity for one worker. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2782":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-41","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command          | Description                              |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `cv report used` | Show used capacity for each live worker. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2783":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-42","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command               | Description                                   |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv report available` | Show available capacity for each live worker. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2784":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-43","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2785":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-44","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"In the current implementation, `cv report capacity <WORKER_ADDRESS>` matches by worker IP address, not by `hostname:port`.","locale":"en"},"2786":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-45","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"**Usage:** `cv node [OPTIONS] [-- <NODES>...]`","locale":"en"},"2787":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-46","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"| Option       | Description                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------------- |\n| `-l, --list` | List live and lost workers. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2788":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-47","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"| Option       | Description                                                |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--versions` | Show release-version distribution across all live workers. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2789":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-48","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"| Option                          | Description                                       |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--add-decommission <NODES>...` | Add one or more workers to the decommission list. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2790":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-49","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"| Option                             | Description                                            |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--remove-decommission <NODES>...` | Remove one or more workers from the decommission list. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2791":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-50","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"`<NODES>` supports two forms:","locale":"en"},"2792":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-51","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"Space-separated arguments: `host1:8997 host2:8997`","locale":"en"},"2793":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-52","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"A single comma-separated argument: `host1:8997,host2:8997`","locale":"en"},"2794":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-53","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2795":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-54","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"`cv node --versions` prints the release-version distribution across live\nworkers, preferring the structured `component_info.release_version` reported on\nheartbeat and falling back to the legacy `software_version` string:","locale":"en"},"2796":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-55","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"See Version Management and Compatibility for the\nmeaning of these versions and how the master evaluates mixed-version peers.","locale":"en"},"2797":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-56","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"The current implementation strips `hostname:port` down to `hostname` before calling the decommission API. The port is mainly for readability and consistent input format.","locale":"en"},"2798":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-57","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"**Usage:** `cv fs [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGS]`","locale":"en"},"2799":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/