lock-size <SIZE>` | Override block size, for example `128MB`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2844":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-103","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                      | Description            |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `-s, --storage-type <TYPE>` | Override storage type. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2845":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-104","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                               | Description                                                               |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--write-type <cache_mode\\|fs_mode>` | The current source only distinguishes these two modes. Default `fs_mode`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2846":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-105","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                                 | Description                             |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `--provider <auto\\|oss-hdfs\\|opendal>` | Select the UFS provider implementation. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2847":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-106","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option    | Description                                                     |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--check` | Only meaningful when listing mounts; also validates each entry. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2848":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-107","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option      | Description                                                                  |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--dry-run` | During `resync`, scan and print differences without delete / create changes. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2849":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-108","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option      | Description                                    |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--verbose` | During `resync`, print detailed per-file logs. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2850":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-109","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"**About `--provider`**: some URI schemes can map to multiple implementations. For example, `oss://...` may be handled either by OSS-HDFS / JindoSDK or by OpenDAL, so `--provider` lets you force the implementation.","locale":"en"},"2851":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-110","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Value  | Description                                         | Typical protocols     |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `auto` | Auto-select implementation based on the URI scheme. | All supported schemes |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"2852":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-111","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Value      | Description                            | Typical protocols |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `oss-hdfs` | Use JindoSDK / OSS-HDFS path handling. | `oss://`          |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"2853":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-112","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Value     | Description                 | Typical protocols                                                                 |\n| --------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `opendal` | Use OpenDAL-based backends. | `s3://`, `oss://`, `hdfs://`, `webhdfs://`, `cos://`, `gcs://`, `azblob://`, etc. |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"2854":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-113","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"There are also a few implementation details worth calling out:","locale":"en"},"2855":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-114","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For `s3://...` paths, if `s3.bucket_name` is not provided explicitly, the CLI auto-fills it from the URI.","locale":"en"},"2856":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-115","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For `hdfs://...` paths, if `hdfs.namenode` / `hdfs.root` are not provided explicitly, the CLI derives them from the URI.","locale":"en"},"2857":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-116","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"If the config contains `hdfs.kerberos.*` keys but neither `hdfs.kerberos.ccache` nor the `KRB5CCNAME` environment variable is present, the CLI prints a Kerberos ticket-cache warning.","locale":"en"},"2858":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-117","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`validate_path_and_configs` currently applies extra path validation only to S3 paths; other schemes mostly rely on later provider initialization and connectivity checks.","locale":"en"},"2859":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-118","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2860":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-119","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For detailed parameter lists of each UFS type (S3, OSS, HDFS, WebHDFS), see Appendix: UFS Mount Parameters at the end.","locale":"en"},"2861":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-120","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`--check-path-consist=true` is enabled by default. That means a path such as `s3://bucket/datasets` is normally expected to mount to `/bucket/datasets`. If you really need a different mapping, pass `--check-path-consist=false` explicitly.","locale":"en"},"2862":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-121","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"In the current source, the first creation of an `fs_mode` mount automatically triggers a `resync`. Manual `cv mount resync ...` only works for `fs_mode` mount points.","locale":"en"},"2863":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-122","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#5-umount-remove-a-mount","content":"**Usage:** `cv umount <CURVINE_PATH>`","locale":"en"},"2864":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-123","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#5-umount-remove-a-mount","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2865":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-124","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"**Usage:** `cv load [OPTIONS] <SOURCE_PATH> [TARGET_PATH]`","locale":"en"},"2866":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-125","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                               |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `<SOURCE_PATH>`   | UFS source URI or a Curvine path below an existing mount. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"2867":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-126","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                                           |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[TARGET_PATH]`   | Optional Curvine destination. A mounted source path derives its target automatically. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"2868":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-127","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                    |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch`     | Watch job status immediately after submission. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"2869":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-128","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `--no-overwrite`  | Fail instead of replacing an existing target. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"2870":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-129","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2871":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-130","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"With Transfer enabled, `load` submits a Transfer job. Otherwise it uses the\nlegacy Master job path. The command prints a job ID and target path in either\nmode.","locale":"en"},"2872":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-131","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"The command line does not change when standalone Transfer is enabled:","locale":"en"},"2873":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-132","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"| Client configuration         | `cv load` / `cv export` route                       |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[transfer] enabled = false` | Legacy Master Load API, for backward compatibility. |","locale":"en","table":"table-9"},"2874":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-133","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"| Client configuration        | `cv load` / `cv export` route                       |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[transfer] enabled = true` | Transfer service RPC, selected directly by the CLI. |","locale":"en","table":"table-9"},"2875":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-134","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"The Transfer service and the client must both be configured for Transfer. Master\nand Worker configuration does not change for a client-side rollout. A client\nwith `transfer.enabled = false` continues to submit through the legacy Master\nAPI.","locale":"en"},"2876":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-135","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"**Usage:** `cv export [OPTIONS] <PATH>`","locale":"en"},"2877":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-136","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"`<PATH>` must be a Curvine path below a mount. Curvine infers the UFS target\nfrom that mount.","locale":"en"},"2878":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-137","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                    |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `<PATH>`          | Curvine source path to export. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"2879":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-138","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                    |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch`     | Watch job status immediately after submission. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"2880":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-139","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                              |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `--no-overwrite`  | Fail when the UFS target already exists. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"2881":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-140","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2882":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-141","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"**Usage:** `cv load-status [OPTIONS] <JOB_ID>`","locale":"en"},"2883":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-142","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description          |\n| ----------------- | -------------------- |\n| `<JOB_ID>`        | Load job identifier. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"2884":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-143","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description     |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `-v, --verbose`   | Verbose output. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"2885":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-144","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument        | Description                                                                 |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch <INTERVAL>` | Poll interval, default `5s`. Supports formats such as `1s`, `1m`, and `1h`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"2886":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-145","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--conf <PATH>`   | Optional one-command config override; normal use does not need it. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"2887":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-146","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2888":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-147","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"In the current implementation, `load-status` enters watch mode by default with a `5s` refresh interval. The source does not currently expose a dedicated one-shot status-only switch.","locale":"en"},"2889":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-148","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"**Usage:** `cv cancel-load [OPTIONS] <JOB_ID>`","locale":"en"},"2890":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-149","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description               |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `<JOB_ID>`        | Job identifier to cancel. |","locale":"en","table":"table-12"},"2891":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-150","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--conf <PATH>`   | Optional one-command config override; normal use does not need it. |","locale":"en","table":"table-12"},"2892":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-151","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2893":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-152","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"`cv transfer` is available only when `[transfer] enabled = true`. It is the\noperations command for listing, inspecting, retrying, and paging Transfer jobs;\nnormal submission remains `cv load` or `cv export`.","locale":"en"},"2894":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-153","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"It requires a reachable Transfer endpoint in the client configuration. See\nTransfer Service for deployment.","locale":"en"},"2895":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-154","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command            | Description                                                                            |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer list` | List jobs. Filter with `--kind load\\|export`, `--state`, `--tenant`, or `--submitter`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2896":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-155","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                       | Description                                                                       |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer status <JOB_ID>` | Show one job. Add `--verbose` for task detail or `--watch --interval 1s` to poll. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2897":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-156","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                      | Description                   |\n| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer tasks <JOB_ID>` | Show a task page for one job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2898":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-157","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                       | Description            |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `cv transfer cancel <JOB_ID>` | Cancel a Transfer job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2899":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-158","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                      | Description                                                         |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer retry <JOB_ID>` | Retry a failed, canceled, or partially successful job as a new job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2900":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-159","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command               | Description               |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer tenants` | Summarize jobs by tenant. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2901":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-160","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2902":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-161","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"`load-status` and `cancel-load` remain compatible shortcuts. With Transfer\nenabled, they call Transfer; with Transfer disabled, they call the legacy\nMaster implementation.","locale":"en"},"2903":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-162","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-version-show-version","content":"**Usage:** `cv version`","locale":"en"},"2904":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-163","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-version-show-version","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2905":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-164","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-version-show-version","content":"The current implementation prints `curvine-cli <version>` together with commit / branch information.","locale":"en"},"2906":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-165","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-version-show-version","content":"Every binary also accepts the global `--version-json` flag to print its full\nstructured version (component, release version, git provenance, protocol\nversion, capabilities) as JSON — see\nVersion Management and Compatibility:","locale":"en"},"2907":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-166","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#12-bench-built-in-benchmark","content":"**Usage:** `cv bench [OPTIONS]` and `cv bench prefill [OPTIONS]`","locale":"en"},"2908":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-167","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#12-bench-built-in-benchmark","content":"`bench` runs metadata and throughput suites against a `cv://` path (client mode)\nor `file://` path (FUSE mode). `cv bench prefill` creates a reusable working set\nfor mixed workloads. Common options include `--path`, `--profile basic|deep`,\n`--mode auto|client|fuse`, `-p/--threads`, `--workload`, `--block-size`,\n`--big-file-size`, and `--big-file-count`. Run `cv bench --help` for the full\noption list.","locale":"en"},"2909":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-168","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#13-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"**Usage:** `cv fsck <PATH> [OPTIONS]`","locale":"en"},"2910":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-169","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#13-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"| Option   | Description                   |\n| -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `<PATH>` | File or directory to inspect. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"2911":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-170","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#13-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"| Option     | Description                                          |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--detail` | Show per-file and per-block details for directories. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"2912":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-171","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#13-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"| Option                 | Description                                                        |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--list-page-size <N>` | Directory entries per listing RPC (default `256`, range `1-4096`). |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"2913":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-172","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#13-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"`fsck` compares the replicas recorded for each block with the replicas currently\navailable and reports under-replicated blocks and read errors. A warning line is\nprinted when the scan finds problems.","locale":"en"},"2914":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-173","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`bin/dfs` in the distribution is a compatibility wrapper:","locale":"en"},"2915":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-174","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"When the first subcommand is `fs` or `report`, it calls Java `io.curvine.CurvineShell`.","locale":"en"},"2916":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-175","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`dfs fs` keeps Hadoop `FsShell` syntax, so subcommands look like `-ls`, `-mkdir`, `-rm -r` with single-dash command names.","locale":"en"},"2917":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-176","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Other subcommands are eventually forwarded to the Rust `curvine-cli`, but for normal operations `cv` is still the recommended entry point.","locale":"en"},"2918":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-177","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2919":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-178","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`dfs report info` is the Java-compat text-summary variant; conceptually it is close to `cv report all`, but the command name is different.","locale":"en"},"2920":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-179","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Use `dfs` when you need Hadoop shell compatibility or rely on Hadoop configuration files such as `core-site.xml` / `hdfs-site.xml`. Use `cv` when you want the full Curvine-native command set from current source.","locale":"en"},"2921":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-180","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Curvine also exposes a FUSE file system interface. After mounting it, for example via `bin/curvine-fuse.sh start`, you can operate on the mount point with normal Linux tools:","locale":"en"},"2922":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-181","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Typical categories:","locale":"en"},"2923":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-182","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Basic file operations: `ls`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm`, `mkdir`","locale":"en"},"2924":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-183","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Content inspection: `cat`, `grep`, `sed`","locale":"en"},"2925":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-184","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"File system information: `df -h`, `du -sh`, `stat`","locale":"en"},"2926":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-185","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Permissions: `chmod`, `chown`","locale":"en"},"2927":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-186","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"If your goal is POSIX compatibility with existing tools, prefer FUSE. If you need Curvine-native mount, load, or node-management features, use `cv`.","locale":"en"},"2928":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-187","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#appendix-ufs-mount-parameters","content":"The following are common parameters passed through `--config key=value` when using `cv mount`. `Required` means it normally must be provided; `Optional` means it can be omitted if a default exists or if the CLI can infer it from the mount URI.","locale":"en"},"2929":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-188","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"Used with `--provider opendal` or auto-selection.","locale":"en"},"2930":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-189","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter         | Required/Optional | Description                                                       |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3.endpoint_url` | Required          | S3 service endpoint URL; must start with `http://` or `https://`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"2931":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-190","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter               | Required/Optional | Description    |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- | -------------- |\n| `s3.credentials.access` | Required          | Access Key ID. |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"2932":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-191","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter               | Required/Optional | Description        |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------ |\n| `s3.credentials.secret` | Required          | Secret Access Key. |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"2933":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-192","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter        | Required/Optional | Description  |\n| ---------------- | ----------------- | ------------ |\n| `s3.region_name` | Optional          | Region name. |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"2934":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-193","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter       | Required/Optional | Description                                                                       |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3.path_style` | Optional          | Whether to use path-style access, commonly needed for MinIO-compatible endpoints. |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"2935":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-194","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"For Alibaba Cloud OSS / OSS-HDFS style access.","locale":"en"},"2936":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-195","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"| Parameter      | Required/Optional | Description           |\n| -------------- | ----------------- | --------------------- |\n| `oss.endpoint` | Required          | OSS endpoint address. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"2937":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-196","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"| Parameter         | Required/Optional | Description                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `oss.accessKeyId` | Required          | Alibaba Cloud AccessKey ID. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"2938":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-197","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"| Parameter             | Required/Optional | Description                     |\n| --------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `oss.accessKeySecret` | Required          | Alibaba Cloud AccessKey Secret. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"2939":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-198","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"| Parameter    | Required/Optional | Description |\n| ------------ | ----------------- | ----------- |\n| `oss.region` | Optional          | Region.     |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"2940":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-199","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter       | Required/Optional | Description                                                          |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hdfs.namenode` | Optional          | NameNode address; if omitted, inferred from the mount URI authority. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"2941":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-200","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter   | Required/Optional | Description                                              |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hdfs.root` | Optional          | Root path; if omitted, inferred from the mount URI path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"2942":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-201","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter   | Required/Optional | Description    |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | -------------- |\n| `hdfs.user` | Optional          | HDFS username. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"2943":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-202","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter               | Required/Optional | Description                             |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `hdfs.atomic_write_dir` | Optional          | Enable atomic write directory behavior. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"2944":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-203","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter              | Required/Optional | Description                                                      |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hdfs.kerberos.ccache` | Optional          | Kerberos credential cache path; can also come from `KRB5CCNAME`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"2945":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-204","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter                 | Required/Optional | Description       |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------- |\n| `hdfs.kerberos.krb5_conf` | Optional          | `krb5.conf` path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"2946":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-205","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter              | Required/Optional | Description  |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------- | ------------ |\n| `hdfs.kerberos.keytab` | Optional          | Keytab path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"2947":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-206","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#webhdfs-webhdfs","content":"| Parameter          | Required/Optional | Description                                                         |\n| ------------------ | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `webhdfs.endpoint` | Optional          | WebHDFS HTTP endpoint; if omitted, inferred from the URI authority. |","locale":"en","table":"table-18"},"2948":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-207","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#webhdfs-webhdfs","content":"| Parameter      | Required/Optional | Description |\n| -------------- | ----------------- | ----------- |\n| `webhdfs.root` | Optional          | Root path.  |","locale":"en","table":"table-18"},"2949":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-208","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#webhdfs-webhdfs","content":"| Parameter            | Required/Optional | Description       |\n| -------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------- |\n| `webhdfs.delegation` | Optional          | Delegation token. |","locale":"en","table":"table-18"},"2950":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations","type":"page","content":"Operations","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations","locale":"en"},"2951":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"page","content":"Monitoring Metrics","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","locale":"en"},"2952":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#metrics-collection","content":"Metrics Collection","locale":"en"},"2953":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#master-metrics","content":"Master Metrics","locale":"en"},"2954":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"Compatibility Metrics","locale":"en"},"2955":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#journal-node-metrics","content":"Journal Node Metrics","locale":"en"},"2956":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#client-metrics","content":"Client Metrics","locale":"en"},"2957":{"id":"/docs/User-M