  | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                         |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Video / model binaries | 256MB - 1GB            | High throughput sequential access |"],[3283,"| Data Pattern        | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                                     |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Small files (< 4MB) | 4MB                    | One block per file, minimal metadata overhead |"],[6656,"| Data Pattern        | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                                     |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Small files (< 4MB) | 4MB                    | One block per file, minimal metadata overhead |"],[3254,"| Data Temperature         | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                   |\n| ------------------------ | ------------ | --- | -------- | ------------------------- |\n| Cold (infrequent access) | HDD          | 30d | 1        | Archives, historical logs |"],[6627,"| Data Temperature         | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                   |\n| ------------------------ | ------------ | --- | -------- | ------------------------- |\n| Cold (infrequent access) | HDD          | 30d | 1        | Archives, historical logs |"],[3253,"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                          |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Warm (regular access) | SSD          | 7d  | 2        | Training datasets, Parquet files |"],[6626,"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                          |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Warm (regular access) | SSD          | 7d  | 2        | Training datasets, Parquet files |"],[3252,"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                       |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Hot (frequent access) | MEM          | 1d  | 2-3      | Model weights, feature tables |"],[6625,"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                       |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Hot (frequent access) | MEM          | 1d  | 2-3      | Model weights, feature tables |"],[2574,"| Dimension           | Curvine Key Point                                                                              |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Product positioning | Distributed file cache with POSIX mounting, with a user experience equivalent to a local disk. |"],[2578,"| Dimension          | Curvine Key Point                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Storage management | Multi-media tiered storage. The client can specify priority, and data falls back automatically when space is insufficient. |"],[2577,"| Dimension         | Curvine Key Point                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Advanced features | Supports extended attributes, symbolic and hard links, timeout-based file locks, sparse files, and preallocation. |"],[2576,"| Dimension        | Curvine Key Point                                                           |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Write capability | Supports random writes and multi-client concurrent writes to the same file. |"],[2579,"| Dimension        | Curvine Key Point                                              |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Space management | `mtime`-based TTL expiration plus optional quota LRU eviction. |"],[2575,"| Dimension       | Curvine Key Point                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Core advantages | Unified namespace, intelligent tiered storage, TTL + LRU space management, and complete POSIX semantics. |"],[2525,"| Feature                             | Description                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Random writes and concurrent writes | Supports writing at any file position. Multiple clients can operate different regions of the same file at the same time, fitting logs, databases, and other flexible write scenarios. |"],[2526,"| Feature                       | Description                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Extended attributes (`xattr`) | Supports file extended attributes, allowing users to store custom metadata for file tagging and business association. |"],[2532,"| Feature                | Description                                                                                                           |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Common file attributes | Basic inode semantics such as permission bits, access/modification timestamps, and truncation follow POSIX standards. |"],[2531,"| Feature             | Description                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Space preallocation | Supports preallocating storage space for files, avoiding insufficient space during large file writes and improving write stability. |"],[2527,"| Feature        | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Symbolic links | Supports symbolic links. It is recommended that link targets point to Curvine internal paths. If a link points to a local path on one machine, other nodes may not be able to access it in a distributed environment. |"],[2530,"| Feature      | Description                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Sparse files | Supports sparse files. Hole regions without actual written data do not occupy physical storage space, saving cluster storage resources. |"],[2529,"| Feature    | Description                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| File locks | Compatible with POSIX locks and BSD locks. In a distributed environment, file locks have a default 5-minute timeout auto-release mechanism to avoid deadlocks caused by abnormal clients or nodes. |"],[2528,"| Feature    | Description                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Hard links | Supports hard links with semantics consistent with local filesystems. This only applies inside the same Curvine filesystem and cannot cross systems. |"],[1247,"| Field                                   | Default | Meaning                                                  |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `master_failed_load_job_retry_interval` | `30s`   | Reuse window for deterministic source-not-found failures |"],[1244,"| Field                                 | Default | Meaning                                  |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `master_max_pending_load_job_submits` | `4096`  | Pending submit requests before admission |"],[1008,"| Field                                 | Default | Meaning                             |\n| ------------------------------------- | ---